{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "guarded_ifelse_inline_not_taken",
    "description": "y[i] = ifelse(i <= 1, 0, ifelse(i > 4, 0, 0.5 (c[i] + c[i-1]))) over 5 nodes, c a inline 4-entry const array. The guards switch the branch off at exactly the cells where c[i] or c[i-1] would be out of range (nodes 1 and 5), so no cell reads one and nothing may fault: node 2 is 15. A binding that evaluates the untaken branch faults here (the chem_vertical_mixing rho_w shape).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "rows": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 4
    },
    "nodes": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 5
    }
  },
  "models": {
